# cli-docs

This package demonstrates how **arb** can generate human-readable documentation
directly from the same schema and data used for code generation.

It shows how command definitions become:

- structured Markdown documentation
- consistent command listings
- example sections derived from data
- man-page style references

No hand-written docs are required once the schema and data are defined.

## How it works

- `schema.yaml` defines the allowed documentation structure
- command and example metadata come from the same data used for code generation
- `templates/` contains Markdown and man-page templates

The output stays consistent with the generated CLI by construction.

## Try it

From the repo root:

```cmd
arb compile --package packages/cli-docs ^
  --data packages/cli-rust/examples/data.nested.yaml ^
  --out out-docs
```

The output will include generated Markdown documentation and a man page.

## Why this exists

Documentation usually drifts out of sync with code.

This package demonstrates how arb treats documentation as another deterministic
output of the same source of truth, instead of a separate manual process.

It is meant as a learning and reference package.
